In vanilla Nethack, armor class seems to affect the accuracy of your
opponents - "the jabberwock misses!" - instead of "the jabberwock tries
to take a bite of your metal plate mail!"

This seems to be different in slash'em, but wouldn't it be more
realistic if attacks would be soaked up by your armor ("The captain
swings his long sword! It hits your body armor!") and have a chance of
damaging your armor too? ("The dwarf swings his dwarvish mattock at
you! The mattock hits your head! It makes a dent in your helmet! You
feel very disoriented.") This would reduce the enchantment of your
armor ("an uncursed -2 dwarvish iron helm (being worn)"), and could
have other effects, too, such as stunning or confusing you.

Of course, sometimes the attacks would miss your armor... ("The ogre
lord swings his club! It hits you right on the neck! -more- Your spinal
cord is severed! You die... do you want your possessions identified?")



